.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-CAPABILITIES" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-capabilities - Set incoming services for a machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine capabilities <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set incoming services for a machine

.PP
Enable or disable incoming terminal, managed SSH, file receive, and preview tunnel services for one machine. Disabled services are not made available simply because the machine is online.

.PP
Machines are account enrollments with independent names, capabilities, and revocation state. Changes target the selected machine, while pb setup configures the current machine. Revocation disconnects an enrollment rather than just hiding it from the list.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--file-receive\fP[=false]
	accept native Inbox transfers

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for capabilities

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--managed-ssh\fP[=false]
	accept managed SSH/SCP/SFTP/rsync

.PP
\fB--preview-tunnel\fP[=false]
	serve preview and tunnel routes

.PP
\fB--terminal\fP[=false]
	accept Paperboat terminal and exec


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
